# PR review / merge gate

Lesson: [#83](https://github.com/mward-sudo/spec_chum/pull/83) merged with unresolved CodeRabbit threads. **Do not repeat that.**

## Hard rule

Unresolved **actionable** CodeRabbit (or similar bot) threads **block merge** unless the user **explicitly** waives them. Ignoring or “finishing” a PR without this gate is a process failure.

## Before merge / when asked to finish or merge a PR

1. Run `./scripts/check_pr_reviews.sh` (or pass the PR number). CI also runs this as **Bot review threads**.
2. Treat bot comments as blocking when **actionable** (bugs, wrong behavior, clear maintainability fixes).
3. Disposition each finding: fix in code, or reply with a short wontfix reason, then **resolve** the thread.
4. Re-run the script (and re-run the CI check if it failed) after addressing feedback.
5. Only waive with user instruction: `--waive "reason"`, `SPEC_CHUM_REVIEW_WAIVER`, or PR label `waive-bot-reviews` — and document the waiver on the PR.

Non-actionable nitpicks may be waived with a one-line reason; do **not** silently ignore Major/functional findings.

See `CONTRIBUTING.md` → “Review check before merge”.
